{"id": "section-body-12468", "title": "Inguinal Bubo (IB)", "chapterId": "chapter-twelve", "blocks": [{"id": "body-12468", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Inguinal Bubo (IB)", "runs": [{"text": "Inguinal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Bubo"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IB)"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1397"}}, {"id": "body-12469", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Inguinal and femoral bubos are localized enlargements of the lymph nodes in the groin area, which are painful and may be fluctuant. They are frequently associated with lymphogranuloma venereum and chancroid. The main Causative agents include Chlamydia trachomatis and Haemophilus ducreyi.", "runs": [{"text": "Inguinal and femoral bubos are localized enlargements of the lymph nodes in the groin area, which are painful and may be fluctuant."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "They"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "frequently"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymphogranuloma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "venereum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chancroid."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "main"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Causative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "agents"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include "}, {"text": "Chlamydia trachomatis ", "italic": true}, {"text": "and "}, {"text": "Haemophilus ducreyi.", "italic": true}]}, {"id": "body-12471", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-12472", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Localized enlargements of the lymph nodes in the groin area,", "runs": [{"text": "Localized"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "enlargements"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lymph"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nodes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "groin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "area,"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12473", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Painful and may be fluctuant.", "runs": [{"text": "Painful"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fluctuant."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12474", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Pain,", "runs": [{"text": "Pain,"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12475", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Fever", "runs": [{"text": "Fever"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12476", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Tenderness.", "runs": [{"text": "Tenderness."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12477-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note", "runs": [{"text": "Note", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-12477-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "In many cases of chancroid an associated genital ulcer is visible, but occasionally may not be.", "runs": [{"text": "In"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "many"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chancroid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "genital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ulcer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "visible,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occasionally"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " be."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1383"}}, {"id": "body-12477-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Non-sexually transmitted local and systemic infections (e.g. infections of the lower limb) can also cause swelling of inguinal lymph nodes. These should therefore be ruled out.", "runs": [{"text": "Non-sexually transmitted local and systemic infections (e.g. infections of the lower limb) can also cause swelling of inguinal lymph nodes. These should therefore be ruled out."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1383"}}, {"id": "body-12479", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-12480", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Culture and Sensitivity", "runs": [{"text": "Culture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Sensitivity"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12481", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "ELISA", "runs": [{"text": "ELISA"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12482", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Quantitative or qualitative PCR", "runs": [{"text": "Quantitative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "qualitative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PCR"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}, {"id": "body-12483", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Direct Fluorescent Antibody (DFA) Management of Inguinal BUBO (see flow chart 12.9)", "runs": [{"text": "Direct Fluorescent Antibody (DFA) Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Inguinal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "BUBO"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "("}, {"text": "see", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "flow", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "chart", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "12.9", "bold": true}, {"text": ")"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1381"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Sexually transmitted infections", "start": "body-12468", "en